## Hard invariants

- Every backend and profile accepts and rejects exactly the same source.
- Borrow validation reads HIR and writes side tables. It does not rewrite HIR or perform backend lowering.
- Lifetime-topology validation is mandatory, backend-independent and profile-independent.
- Every allocation family has exactly one semantic lifetime owner.
- GC cannot bypass topology validation or legalise invalid retained edges.
- A capable full-control release backend must not fall back to a tracing or reachability collector.
- A missing physical strategy after successful topology validation is `CompilerError`.
- Affine cleanup responsibility may move or be discharged, but it never duplicates.
- For one REC-selected family `F`, `REC count(F) = live counted persistent-edge obligations(F) + optional affine-root obligation(F)`, where the affine-root term is zero or one. Ordinary aliases, parameters, temporary projections and `get()` results never contribute obligations, and REC never establishes legality.
- Declared-region-owned storage is count-free, is never released individually and is the only source mechanism for cycles. Count-free describes the declared region's own targets: an edge from declared-region-owned storage into an externally owned REC family is still a counted edge into that external family, released at declared-region exit before bulk reclamation.
- Backends receive validated topology and a memory plan, and may not reconsider source legality.
- No compiler or backend path may rely on unchecked aliasing or undefined behaviour to make the memory model work.
